----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `WidgetDetailCard` is a PURE presentational widget primitive (a shared widget building block): it
  takes `entries: DetailEntry[]` + optional `compact` / `emptyMessage` / `emptyIcon` and renders a
  scrollable column of label/value rows. Each row = an uppercase muted label (web `text-[10px] uppercase
  tracking-wide`) on the leading edge and, trailing, the formatted value (web `value ?? '—'`, monospaced
  when `mono`) followed by an optional `<Badge>`. A hairline separator sits below every row except the last
  (web `i < visible.length - 1`). It condenses to the first four entries when `compact` (web
  `entries.slice(0, 4)`), scrolls within the host height (web `overflow-y-auto h-full`), and falls back to
  `<EmptyState icon message={emptyMessage ?? 'No details available'} />` when `entries.length === 0`.
  There is NO fetch / React-Query / Promise in the source, so it has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch
  (the host widget that owns the query renders those). Per the sibling presentational-primitive precedent
  (WidgetComparisonCard 0003, WidgetTipCards 0012, Delta 0081, MetricCard 0095) this surface reproduces
  ONLY the source's REAL branches:
    • populated column (one row per visible entry; uppercase label + value + optional mono + optional badge)
    • compact slice    (the first four entries; web `compact ? entries.slice(0, 4) : entries`)
    • em-dash fallback  (a row whose value is nil renders "—"; web `entry.value ?? '—'`)
    • empty leaf        (friendly "never a blank box" peer of web <EmptyState> — default "No details available")
  The badge REUSES the shared native `TSBadge` (web `Badge`) with the web `badgeVariantMap` tone
  (success -> success, warning -> warning, error -> danger, neutral -> neutral). The empty leaf REUSES the
  shared native `TSEmptyState` (web `EmptyState` from `@/components/feedback`).
  Files: WidgetDetailCard.Adapter/Model/.swift/Views/Previews/Tests/AdapterTests.swift + .strings.
  Bindings : P1/S8 WidgetDetailCardModel @Observable holder (props + projection; no HTTP in the view);
             P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius/TSTypeMetrics) — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex;
             P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade (table "WidgetDetailCard"); P1/S11 view.opened telemetry
             (slug "WidgetDetailCard", emitted once + idempotent across appear/disappear).
  i18n     : web source has 0 t() keys (anonymous; its only literals "No details available" + the em-dash
             value fallback are reproduced via widgetDetailCard.empty + widgetDetailCard.valueFallback).
             Native a11y/HIG additions: emptyHint, rowLabel, rowLabelWithBadge. 5 keys total, 0 dead keys.
  a11y     : each row folds into one VoiceOver element reading "{label}, {value}, {badge}" (badge omitted
             when absent); the label uses the `label` type role + token tracking + .textCase(.uppercase)
             (Dynamic Type, not a hardcoded 10px); the populated column is an accessibility container; the
             empty leaf is a ContentUnavailableView. Reduce-Motion-safe (no animations introduced).

